  "foaf:name": "EmpowerCoast Digital Twin",
  "sdo:name": "EmpowerCoast Digital Twin",
  "sdo:description": "The EmpowerCoast Digital Twin (DT) (https://researchproject.educationhost.co.uk/landing) is a prototype built to show how technology can work for people, not just alongside them. Developed through the EmpowerUs Horizon project, it was designed with a single purpose: to help coastal communities see their own coastal futures more clearly, and to give them the spatial evidence they need to shape it. Rather than producing another static map or report that risks being unnoticed by common citizens, the EmpowerCoast DT is alive. It draws on spatial data, IoT sensors, and predictive modelling, and brings them together in a way that is directly relevant to the EmpowerUs Transition Coastal Labs (TCLs). This Digital Twin is not just another piece of technology. It is a coastal resilience and policy-accelerating tool that keeps decision-making anchored in evidence. TThe platform makes knowledge accessible to all, turning the EmpowerUs vision of ‘Leave no one behind’ into practice.",
  "sdo:location": "Ireland",
  "sdo:identifier": "89.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/empowercoast-digital-twin/",
